   "says": "Failures become lessons; lessons become playbook; a better playbook means fewer failures and flaws."
  },
  {
   "id": "B-decay",
   "polarity": "balancing",
   "stocks": [
    "t_playbook",
    "t_landed_recent"
   ],
   "says": "The playbook goes stale as the code it describes changes; the faster we land, the faster it rots."
  },
  {
   "id": "B-overload",
   "polarity": "balancing",
   "stocks": [
    "t_playbook"
   ],
   "says": "Past about 120 entries a bigger playbook lowers success: too much context."
  },
  {
   "id": "R-trap",
   "polarity": "reinforcing",
   "stocks": [
    "t_open",
    "t_lessons",
    "t_playbook"
   ],
   "says": "When the backlog is long, lessons are not captured; the playbook decays; more work fails; the backlog grows."
  },
  {
   "id": "B-trust",
   "polarity": "balancing",
   "stocks": [
    "t_trust",
    "t_check_flawed",
    "t_review_flawed",
    "t_latent",
    "t_bugs"
   ],
   "says": "Clean landings raise trust; trust lowers how much I check; more flaws escape; late findings cut trust."
  },
  {
   "id": "B-fatigue",
   "polarity": "balancing",
   "stocks": [
    "t_review_sound",
    "t_review_flawed"
   ],
   "says": "A long review queue slows reviewers and lowers how many flaws they catch."
  },
  {
   "id": "R-debt",
   "polarity": "reinforcing",
   "stocks": [
    "t_debt",
    "t_attempted",
    "t_latent"
   ],
   "says": "Landings, especially flawed ones, add debt; debt slows attempts and raises flaws; paying it down competes for agents."
  },
  {
   "id": "R-reputation",
   "polarity": "reinforcing",
   "stocks": [
    "t_reputation",
    "t_asks",
    "t_landed_recent"
   ],
   "says": "Delivering builds requesters' confidence, which brings more asks; bugs erode it."
  }
 ],
 "id": "story-1-simple-task",
 "name": "Story 1: simple tasks, done by agents that learn",
 "description": "Other teams ask me for simple tasks. I collect the requirements; agents research, write the ticket, attempt it, and learn from failures by writing their own playbook. Whether an attempt succeeds, fails, or hides a flaw depends on the playbook and the code's debt. My trust in the agents decides how much I check; what I don't check goes to the company, whose checks and reviewers catch some flaws and miss others, which land and come back as bugs. Delivering builds requesters' confidence, which brings more asks. Time unit: a working hour; horizon 26 weeks.",
 "time_unit": "working hour",
 "horizon": 1040,
